  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "Independent comparison confirms the transport formula, characteristic geometry, classical PDE branch and flux signs. The remaining issues concern the source's unspecified nonsmooth meaning and an incompletely exposed measure dependency; they cannot be settled by agreement between judges.",
      "primary_evidence": "Attached printed page 1, equations (1.2)-(1.3); printed pages 4-5, equation (1.10) and section 1.1.2; target type and D001-D004."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The blind translation correctly reconstructs all five conjuncts, including the independent antecedents and the integrability requirements inside rectangle conservation. Its uncertainty about the measure is supported by the supplied declaration evidence.",
      "primary_evidence": "The readable and explicit target types, blind LocalDef001-LocalDef004, direct D001-D004, D024, D028, D055 and D081."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined because exact source equivalence remains unestablished. The differentiability and integrability antecedents are not grounds for faithful-stronger classification.",
      "primary_evidence": "Target's fourth and fifth conjuncts; printed page 1's arbitrary-profile assertion and printed pages 4-5's qualitative smoothness and discontinuity discussion."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined. The translation introduces no demonstrable sign, object or quantifier error, but the supplied evidence does not fix every semantic bridge needed for acceptance.",
      "primary_evidence": "Blind translation's five conclusions compared with the target type and equations (1.2), (1.3) and (1.10)."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D055 unclear",
      "resolution": "The dependency fixes one particular measure, but its displayed body, inferInstance, does not expose the selected instance or its normalization. D028 only projects that measure. The direct judge's acceptance at a library trust boundary is an assumption, not additional declaration evidence resolving this dispute. Preserve this evidence gap without alleging an incorrect actual measure.",
      "primary_evidence": "D055 has type MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace Real and body inferInstance in both dossiers; D028 has body fun α [self] => self.2. No supplied reuse entry resolves D055."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D002 unclear",
      "resolution": "Its Lean meaning is resolved: it conjoins integrability of all spatial slices, integrability of all temporal flux traces and an exact oriented rectangle balance. It contains no assertion that interval mass has an ordinary derivative everywhere. Its equivalence to the source's nonsmooth interpretation remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002's complete definition body; printed page 4 equation (1.10) and printed page 5's continuation of section 1.1.2."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D024 unclear",
      "resolution": "Its Lean meaning is resolved: integrability on both (a,b] and (b,a] for the fixed measure. Under ordinary length measure, universal quantification over finite endpoints gives local absolute integrability, without finite total mass or decay requirements. This condition is necessary for D002 itself because its spatial integrability requirement at time zero recovers profile integrability.",
      "primary_evidence": "D024's definition, D002's first conjunct, D003 evaluated at t=0 and the target's first conjunct."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "Global profile differentiability is exactly necessary for the target's everywhere classical predicate: the spatial slice at time zero is the profile. It is therefore not an arbitrary extra restriction within that predicate. Likewise, profile interval integrability is necessary for the chosen rectangle predicate. Neither necessity establishes that the source intended precisely these predicates.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 and D004 require an actual spatial derivative at every x and t; D003 gives q(x,0)=profile(x); D002 requires spatial integrability at t=0."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "Initial data, unchanged shape, constant-speed propagation and classical satisfaction on differentiable profiles are represented. The unconditional characteristic derivative is a consequence of constancy and adds no missing classical partial derivative. Completeness of the broader nonsmooth solution assertion remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "Target conjuncts one through four, D003-D004, printed page 1 equation (1.3) and printed page 5's exclusion of classical PDE satisfaction at discontinuities."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "Under ordinary length measure, rectangle balance gives locally absolutely continuous interval mass and the displayed endpoint-flux derivative equality almost everywhere for each fixed spatial interval. An almost-everywhere derivative equality alone does not generally recover rectangle balance without absolute continuity or a suitable distributional formulation. Thus unrestricted equivalence with a derivative-form assertion cannot be assumed.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002 identifies M(t)-M(s) with the integral of an interval-integrable flux difference; equation (1.10) displays M'(t) without specifying exceptional times or absolute continuity."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "No scalar-field, dimension, velocity-sign or time-domain specialization appears. The only disputed applicability choice is the precise nonsmooth solution domain. It must remain explicit and cannot count as genuine additional strength.",
      "primary_evidence": "Explicit target binders are Real throughout; printed page 1 specializes m=1 and states no sign or time restriction; the fifth target conjunct has an interval-integrability antecedent."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Zero speed and reversed or coincident endpoints are coherently included. The transported-step counterexample is valid: with p(ξ)=1 for ξ>0 and 0 otherwise, c=1 and spatial interval [0,1], M(t)=1 for negative t near zero and M(t)=1-t for positive t near zero. M is not differentiable at zero. This excludes an everywhere-classical reading of nonsmooth equation (1.10), but does not select a unique replacement interpretation.",
      "primary_evidence": "Equation (1.3), equation (1.10), D003 and D081's oriented integration definition; printed page 5 asserts persistence of integral conservation at discontinuities."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The target verifies an explicit family and introduces neither uniqueness nor a converse classifying arbitrary solutions. Its classical effective domain is differentiable profiles; its rectangle predicate necessarily requires interval-integrable profiles. Exact preservation of the source's nonsmooth domain remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "Target's universal profile and speed binders, D001-D004 and printed page 1's assertion that the equation admits the displayed family."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation correctly keeps the two regularity antecedents separate and leaves all geometric clauses unconditional. Their necessity for the selected global solution predicates is established from the time-zero slice; attributing those precise admissibility classes to the source remains unsupported.",
      "primary_evidence": "Blind translation's hypotheses, elaborated target conjunction structure, D002-D004 and printed pages 1 and 4-5."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "No conjunct was lost in back-translation. The remaining completeness question belongs to the comparison of the chosen rectangle solution notion with the source, rather than to translation accuracy.",
      "primary_evidence": "Blind translation's conclusions reproduce all target conjuncts and all three components of D002; printed pages 4-5 do not define rectangle conservation explicitly."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The supplied bodies resolve the translation, derivative predicates, arithmetic, conjunctions, witness scope, interval integrability and orientation. Reuse records preserve those meanings without deciding current source correspondence. D055's selected measure remains insufficiently exposed for the disputed identification with dx and dt.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001-D004, D012, D014, D018, D022, D024, D028, D055, D073, D077, D080-D081 and D090, together with the supplied reuse ledger."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation correctly states finite-time balance, not an everywhere derivative law. Smooth profiles permit the usual differential interpretation under ordinary length measure; discontinuous profiles require a qualified temporal interpretation. The source does not specify which precise interpretation governs all admitted profiles.",
      "primary_evidence": "Blind translation's fifth conclusion, D002 and printed pages 4-5, equation (1.10) and section 1.1.2."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The integrability premise is local over every finite interval, not global integrability over the real line. This resolves a possible excessive restriction. Whether even this local domain exactly matches the source's intended arbitrary profiles remains uncertain.",
      "primary_evidence": "D024 and the fifth target antecedent quantify finite real endpoints; printed page 1 gives no function-space specification."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Orientation consistently extends ordered-interval balances to reversed endpoints, and equal endpoints yield legitimate zero identities. For nonzero speed, null-set changes to a locally integrable profile affect each temporal trace only on a null set under ordinary length measure; for zero speed the flux is identically zero. These facts support the chosen formulation but do not establish the source's precise exceptional-time convention.",
      "primary_evidence": "D003 gives affine temporal traces, the target flux is speed times state, and D081 subtracts integrals over oppositely oriented half-open intervals."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "There is no uniqueness or well-posedness overclaim. Nonvacuity holds for the classical branch with p(ξ)=ξ and c=1. Under ordinary length measure, the same profile activates both branches, and a step profile activates the nonsmooth conservation branch. Nonvacuity of substantive integral examples in the exact encoded measure remains conditional on resolving D055.",
      "primary_evidence": "D003-D004 and the target's independent implications; D002 and D024 for the integral branch; D055 for the outstanding measure identification."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication lean_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "The geometric and classical portions are confirmed. The complete direction remains unclear because Lean guarantees rectangle conservation only on its stated integrability domain and does not assert an everywhere mass derivative; the source does not fix the corresponding nonsmooth domain and temporal meaning.",
      "primary_evidence": "Target type, D002-D004, printed page 1 equations (1.2)-(1.3) and printed pages 4-5."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication source_implies_lean unclear",
      "resolution": "The source formula yields the geometric clauses and, by ordinary differentiation, the classical clause. Under ordinary length measure, change of variables and interval additivity also yield the rectangle clause for locally integrable profiles. This establishes its mathematical justification under that interpretation, but does not resolve D055 or establish that the source's stated nonsmooth notion is exactly this formulation.",
      "primary_evidence": "Equation (1.3), D003, D002, D024 and D081; D055 exposes only inferInstance."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "The back-translation adds no independent obstacle beyond the direct comparison. Its unspecified fixed measure and precise conditional rectangle formulation leave the complete implication unclear, while its transport geometry and classical branch match.",
      "primary_evidence": "Blind translation's mathematical definitions and conclusions compared with D001-D004 and equations (1.2), (1.3) and (1.10)."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "The reverse direction is justified for the geometric and classical clauses and conditionally justified for the integral clause when μ is ordinary length measure. A conclusive source-faithfulness implication still requires the missing measure evidence and a fixed interpretation of nonsmooth conservation.",
      "primary_evidence": "Blind translation explicitly denotes the unresolved measure by μ; D055's body is inferInstance; printed pages 4-5 do not specify a precise weak-solution definition."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "The exact real scalar translation, constant speed, unchanged shape and classical advection for differentiable profiles are preserved. The rectangle clause gives a substantive conservation statement on its explicit integrability domain. Under ordinary length measure it implies an almost-everywhere mass derivative identity for each fixed interval, but not an everywhere identity. Neither the source's full nonsmooth admissibility class nor its precise temporal interpretation is fixed by the selected pages. The disputed identification of D055 with ordinary length measure also remains unverified from the supplied declarations."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Equation (1.3) supplies initial data, characteristic constancy and its zero derivative; differentiation supplies the classical PDE clause. With ordinary length measure and the target's interval-integrability antecedent, affine change of variables and interval additivity justify the rectangle clause, including its slice and flux integrability requirements. This conditional mathematical derivation does not resolve the exact measure dependency or establish equivalence of the source's unspecified nonsmooth solution meaning with the chosen rectangle formulation."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "D055 does not expose the instance selected by inferInstance or establish its identification with normalized ordinary length measure. No incorrect measure has been demonstrated.",
    "The selected source pages do not determine whether locally absolutely integrable profiles exhaust the intended admissible nonsmooth profiles.",
    "The source retains equation (1.10) at discontinuities without specifying a time-integrated, distributional or appropriately qualified derivative interpretation. An everywhere-classical interpretation is ruled out by the transported-step example."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unresolved-measure-evidence",
      "evidence": "D028 merely projects the measure from D055; D055 is displayed only as inferInstance in both dossiers and has no supplied validated meaning-reuse entry.",
      "impact": "The exact integration measure cannot be conclusively matched to the source's dx and dt under the requested evidence-bound dependency review."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unresolved-source-solution-semantics",
      "evidence": "Printed page 1 gives arbitrary-profile language after (1.3), while printed pages 4-5 retain integral conservation at discontinuities without a precise admissibility class or temporal convention. D002 fixes integrability and time-integrated rectangle balance.",
      "impact": "The target is a mathematically justified precise formulation under ordinary length measure, but exact equivalence to the selected source assertion remains unestablished."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "effective-domain-and-strength",
      "evidence": "D004 at time zero requires profile differentiability, and D002 at time zero requires profile interval integrability. The target supplies these as separate antecedents.",
      "impact": "These conditions are necessary for the selected predicates rather than gratuitous restrictions within them. They still cannot be credited as stronger applicability relative to an unspecified source domain."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "nonvacuity-and-characteristic-derivative",
      "evidence": "D003 makes every characteristic composite identically profile(x), and p(ξ)=ξ with speed 1 gives a nonconstant classical solution. Under ordinary length measure, smooth and step profiles activate substantive rectangle balances.",
      "impact": "No impossible classical premise, totalized-derivative shortcut or confusion between characteristic and coordinate derivatives was found. Substantive integral nonvacuity is established conditionally on the measure identification."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Independent inspection of the attached primary-source renderings and inline declaration evidence confirms the transport construction and resolves the meanings and effective domains of the disputed solution predicates. The transported-step example rules out treating nonsmooth integral conservation as an everywhere-classical mass derivative identity. It does not authorize choosing a unique weak interpretation absent from the source. The supplied measure declaration also does not resolve the specific dependency dispute. Consequently, undetermined with acceptance withheld is consistent with both implication assessments; no majority vote or claim of genuine strengthening is used. No tools were used, and source-byte or rendering hashes were not independently recomputed."
}
